  "lineage": "Saidi music of Upper Egypt (south of Cairo extending to Aswan), the canonical pre-modern rural musical tradition of the Egyptian Nile Valley peasant Saidi communities. Performance centers on the mizmar pair (loud double-reed conical-bore aerophone played in heterophonic-melodic-elaboration) over tabla baladi or tabla dohola two-headed barrel-drum. Repertoire spans wedding-celebration cycles, mawwal vocal-lament solo declamations (free-rhythm extended-melismatic-ornament register), and tahtib stick-dance accompaniment cycles for which Saidi music is particularly known.",
